          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Lawvere distribution
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosheaf"} cosheaf
            valued in some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %em Lawvere distribution
            is a kind of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of the concept of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
          %p
            To some extent one may think of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            as being a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on that space: to each point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            it assigns the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* F \in Set
            %em Lawvere distribution
            is the analog of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
            in the sense of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+linear+functional"} continuous linear functional
            = succeed "-preserving" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            of sets as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            (under set
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/numbers"} numbers
            and hence read preservation of colimits as
            %em linearity
            \.)
          %p
            Better yet, under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+cardinality"} ∞-groupoid cardinality
            we may think of tame
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            and hence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            as a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of real-number valued functions. This yields a more general notion of Lawvere distributions on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            preserving
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
          %p
            Still more generally one may allow to generalize
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} locally presentable (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pr(\infty,1)Cat
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category of presentable (∞,1)-categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Throughout
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            is some base
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            and all notions are to be understood as indexed over this base.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              (Lawvere, see Definition 1.3.4 in
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "#SCT"} Bunge and Funk
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              (more generally, over an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
              %strong distribution
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              with values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
              is an
              %span.newWikiWord
                (∞,1)-cosheaf
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-cosheaf"} ?
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              with values in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{K}
            %p
              that preserves
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Dist
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Dist_S(\mathcal{E}, \mathcal{K}) \subset (\infty,1)Func(\mathcal{E}, \mathcal{K})
            %p
              for the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-functors
              on those that are
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  (∞,1)-cosheaves
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-cosheaves"} ?
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor+theorem"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor theorem
              this is equivalently a pair
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mu \dashv \mu^*) : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{K}
            %p
              of (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              \-indexed)
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
          .un_remark
            %h6#notation Notation
            %p
              To amplify the interpretation in analogy with
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
              one sometimes writes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi d
                    %mi μ
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int_{\mathcal{E}} (-) d\mu : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{K}
            %p
              for a Lawvere distribution
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            %p
              Notably in the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K} =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(F)
              is tame, we may use
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mi F
                    %mi d
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int_{\mathcal{E}} F d \mu \in \mathbb{R}
            %p
              for the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+cardinality"} ∞-groupoid cardinality
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#DiracDeltaDistribution
            Dirac
            = succeed "-distributions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} point of a topos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (p^* \dashv p_*) : \mathcal{S} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} \mathcal{E}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
            is therefore a Lawvere distribution. This sends any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            at the point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+distribution"} Dirac distribution
            on functions.
          %h3#the_canonical_distribution_on_a_locally_connected_topos
            The canonical distribution on a locally
            = succeed "-connected" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            then its terminal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-geometric+morphism"} (∞,1)-geometric morphism
            by definition has a further left adjoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Δ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 0
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi \dashv \Delta \dashv \Gamma) : \mathcal{E} \stackrel{\overset{\Pi_0}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Delta}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}}
                  \\mathcal{S}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+in+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid in a locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int_{\mathcal{E}}(-) d x : \mathcal{E} \to \infty Grpd
                  \\,.
          %p
            This construction also works in the relative setting: if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\colon E\to K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+geometric+morphism"} locally ∞-connected geometric morphism
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_!\colon E\to K
            is a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h3#local_toposes Local toposes
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} local (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\colon E\to K
            is a
            %span.newWikiWord
              local (∞,1)-geometric morphism
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-geometric+morphism"} ?
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_*
            is a (left exact) Lawvere distribution on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h3#multiplication_of_distributions_by_functions Multiplication of distributions by functions
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in \mathcal{E}
            an
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{S}
            a distribution, there is a new distribution
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi μ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \cdot \mu :
                  G \mapsto
                  \\mu(F \times G)
                  \\,.
          %p In the functional notation this is the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mi G
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ×
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int_{\mathcal{E}} G d(F \times \mu)
                  \=
                  \\int_{\mathcal{E}} G \times F d \mu
                  \\,.
          %h3#distributions_on_the_point Distributions on the point
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd \simeq Sh_{(\infty,1)}(*)
            itself coincide with the value at the single point
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Dist
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Dist(\infty Grpd, \infty Grpd) \simeq \infty Grpd.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+topos"} symmetric topos
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bagdomain+topos"} bagdomain topos
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosheaf"} cosheaf
          %p
            For the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(∞,1)Cat
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The 1-categorical notion has been described by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            in a series of talks and expositions. For instance in the context of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
              ,
              %em Axiomatic cohesion
              , Theory and Applications of Categories, Vol. 19, No. 3, 2007, pp. 41–49. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/19/3/19-03.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A comprehensive discussion is in
          %ul
            %li#SCT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"} Marta Bunge
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathon+Funk"} Jonathon Funk
              %em Singular coverings of toposes
              , Lecture Notes in Mathematics vol. 1890 Springer Heidelberg (2006). (chap. 1)
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                %em Cosheaves and Distributions on Toposes
                , Alg. Univ.
                %strong 34
                (1995) pp.469-484.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathon+Funk"} Jonathon Funk
                %em Spreads and the Symmetric Topos
                , JPAA
                %strong 113
                (1996) pp.1-38.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathon+Funk"} Jonathon Funk
                %em Spreads and the Symmetric Topos II
                , JPAA
                %strong 130
                (1998) pp.49-84.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gonzalo+E.+Reyes"} Gonzalo E. Reyes
                %em A Note on Frame Distributions
                , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
                %strong 40
                (1999) pp.127-140.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Pitts"}> Andrew Pitts
                ,
                %em On Product and Change of Base for Toposes
                , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
                %strong 26
                (1985) pp.43-61.
